From: junkyard
Subject: [PATCH] aoc: don't pull Laguna's arm-smmu-v3 module into gs201 builds

aoc_core depends on //private/google-modules/iommu/arm-smmu-v3 for
pixel-iommu-fault.ko. Only Laguna adds that package's Kconfig
(lga_defconfig: ARM_SMMU_V3_PIXEL, GOOGLE_ACFW_DEBUG, ...); on gs201 the
symbols do not exist, the kernel_module builds none of its five declared
outs, and the lynx dist fails:

  ERROR: Unable to find acfw-debug.ko ... arm_smmu_v3.ko ...
         pixel-iommu-fault.ko in .../iommu/arm-smmu-v3

Depend on that module only for soc_is_laguna_or_later; keep the
header-only fault_headers everywhere. On gs201 the pixel_iommu_*() fault
API aoc.c calls is provided by samsung_iommu.ko (gs201_soc, which aoc_core
already depends on), so aoc.c itself is unchanged.
---
diff --git a/BUILD.bazel b/BUILD.bazel
index 2fe1e09..e9bee63 100644
--- a/BUILD.bazel
+++ b/BUILD.bazel
@@ -80,7 +80,6 @@ ddk_module(
         "//private/google-modules/aoc:__subpackages__",
     ],
     deps = [
-        "//private/google-modules/iommu/arm-smmu-v3",
         "//private/google-modules/iommu/arm-smmu-v3:fault_headers",
         "//common:all_headers_aarch64",
         "//private/google-modules/aoc_ipc:ddk_headers",
@@ -90,6 +89,9 @@ ddk_module(
         "//private/google-modules/trusty:trusty_headers",
     ] + select({
         "//private/devices/google/common:soc_is_laguna_or_later": [
+            # Only Laguna configures arm-smmu-v3 (lga_defconfig); on older SoCs
+            # its Kconfig is absent and it builds none of its declared outs.
+            "//private/google-modules/iommu/arm-smmu-v3",
             "//private/google-modules/soc/rdo:rdo_soc_headers",
             "//private/google-modules/soc/rdo:rdo_soc_module",
         ],
